# The neighbor matrix in a narrow tilted cell that a barostat shrinks until
# the pairlist distance is well beyond half of the least of a_x, b_y, c_z
# (#258, D241, docs/triclinic-m2.md, Section 2): at every frame
# the potential energy of `mdir run` is the sum over every image of every
# pair within the cutoff (Inputs/triclinic_reach.py). The build that tested
# the image of the one pass alone lost pairs in 9 of the 79 frames.
#
# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/triclinic_reach.py %t mdir CPU MATRIX | FileCheck %s

# CHECK:      79 frames, 79 with the reach beyond half of the least of the diagonal
# CHECK-NEXT: half of the least of the diagonal well below the reach
# CHECK-NEXT: frames whose potential is not the sum over all images: 0
